  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "Register: who says what",
   "text": "In speech many people drop the internal augment and say *υπόγραψε, παράδωσε, ανάλαβε*, or sidestep it with the long ending or a periphrasis (*εκλέξανε*, *έκανε κατάθεση*). These forms are fine in a kafeneio but sound uneducated in an interview, a meeting or an essay. At C1 you are expected to use the internal augment in writing and in formal speech, and to recognise the learned passive pasts below in every news bulletin."
